# Ice and glass far from the camera turn back into terrain (C138), in the
# terrain of a 4096x4096 world, with a target of four blocks in memory as
# terrain_bodies. A body of ice, one of glass that does not shatter and
# one of glass that shatters drop onto the ground right of the middle of
# the view; they crack where they land, and the glass that shatters turns
# into powder. Once they sleep, the camera walks right, 128 cells every 10
# ticks: when its middle has moved more than 512 cells, the ice and the
# glass that does not shatter, pieces too, asleep 350 or more cells away,
# turn back into cells of ice and glass, one for each pixel. The camera
# walks back, and the tool digs the glass the slab left: what is left
# around the hole turns into static bodies again. Cells come and go with
# their blocks, so this replay is not checked for conservation.
